        {
          "id": 1989948462,
          "type": null,
          "body": "The [man page for ares-library-init](https://c-ares.org/docs/ares_library_init.html) says:\n\n> Successive calls to this function do nothing further, only the first call done when c-ares is in an uninitialized state is actually effective. \n\nAre you able to share some evidence that this is a memory leak, and that the documentation is in error or misleading?",
